IN THE COURT OF ADDITIONAL SESSIONS JUDGE, SAKET COURTS, NEW DELHI
BAIL APPLICATION NO: BA-882/2026 IN FIR NO: 124/2026 SAKET PS
CASE TITLE: STATE VS. RAJESH KUMAR
================================================================================

ORDER ON BAIL APPLICATION:
1. Present application under Section 439 Cr.P.C. / BNS Section 483 has been filed on behalf of applicant/accused Rajesh Kumar seeking grant of regular bail in FIR No. 124/2026 registered under BNS Section 103, 318, and 336.

2. Learned Senior Counsel Advocate A. Verma submitted that the accused is innocent and has been falsely implicated due to civil property disputes.

3. Learned Public Prosecutor strongly opposed the bail application, submitting that the CFSL forensic lab report confirms accused fingerprints on the murder weapon, and stolen cash INR 4,50,000 along with forged property land deeds were recovered directly from accused premises under CrPC 102 seizure memo.

4. FINDINGS & ORDER:
   Considering the grave nature of homicide charges under BNS Section 103, strong forensic corroboration, and potential risk of accused influencing eyewitness Ramesh Kumar or tampering with original land registry files, this Court finds no merit in the bail application.

   Bail application is accordingly DISMISSED.

DATED: 18/08/2026
PRESIDING JUDGE: Hon. Justice A.K. Mehra, Additional Sessions Judge, Saket Courts
[Official Judicial Seal Attached]
